    "fridgeDays": 1,
    "feel": "Sweet summer stone fruit with a sneaky chilli-honey kick — sophisticated and a little surprising.",
    "didYouKnow": "Hot honey feels like an invention of the 2010s, but southern Italian farmers were steeping chillies in honey — miele piccante — to drizzle over sharp cheese generations before an American pizzeria put a squeeze bottle of it on every table and set off a worldwide craze. Peaches and nectarines are 'stone fruit', drupes built around a single hard pip, and a thread of chilli heat makes their sweetness ring louder.",
